+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""set4: a narrow re-measurement of what commit 557b554eb ("Corrections from the final native round") changed, with
+real services on disposable QEMU guests (lab.py).
+
+Two cell kinds, both built on the drivers of set3 and changing none of them:
+
+``set4-arch`` | ``set4-debian13`` | ``set4-ubuntu`` (``Set4Trial`` over ``request_identity_trial.RequestIdentityTrial``):
+the candidate is installed fresh and the owner's setup is run exactly as in the ``rid3-*`` cells (steps preflight,
+origin, baseline-install, owner-login, license, setup, site); then, as the logged-in owner,
+
+  M0  the platform as it stands, the lab's isolation, the nginx package's PHP snippet and its digest (item 7);
+  M1  a PHP site: created through the Panel, ``nginx -t``, one PHP page executed as the site's own account, a missing
+      script, PATH_INFO, the PHP version and the PHP-FPM socket the Panel recorded, the site deleted and what is left
+      (items 1, 3, 8);
+  M2  the cPanel-archive import of set3's fixture, and the imported site served (items 2, 3);
+  M5  an archive with a member named by an absolute path (item 5);
+  M10 Postfix stopped through the Panel while ``postfix check`` refuses ``main.cf`` (item 10; mail platforms);
+  M4  a Reload of a stopped nginx, MariaDB and PostgreSQL through the Panel (item 4);
+  M6  a new site whose configuration the web server refuses (item 6): one reading after the owner moved nginx's own
+      ``fastcgi.conf`` away, one with a long site name and no owner action. M6 runs right after M1, while no PHP
+      site exists.
+
+``upd1-*`` (``Set4UpdateTrial`` over ``owner_update_trial.Trial``): the owner-started update of set3 with two added
+steps. Good cells: a PHP site is created by the installed baseline before the update and asked a fixed set of
+requests; after the verified update the same requests are asked again, the site's General settings are saved once
+through the Panel (which renders the vhost again) and the requests are asked a third time (item 9). Rollback cells:
+after the automatic return the update check is read and recorded raw, with what the served web build holds (item 12).
+
+The driver calls only the Panel's HTTP API; every native fact is read over SSH by ``guest_set4_native.py`` and the
+set3 helpers, and what the owner does on the server by hand goes through ``owner-*`` modes and is recorded as such.
+No certificate authority and no licence service is contacted. Every result carries ``native_evidence: false``.
+
+  set4_trial.py plan --cell set4-arch --artifacts A.json --work-root /var/tmp/cp-release-drill-X [--dry-run]
+  set4_trial.py run  --cell set4-arch --artifacts A.json --work-root /var/tmp/cp-release-drill-X --execute
+"""
